                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 25 at 11:57AM MDT until October 26 at 6:00AM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of east central, northeast, and southeast New\nMexico, including the following areas, in east central New Mexico,\nDe Baca County, Guadalupe County and Roosevelt County. In northeast\nNew Mexico, Eastern San Miguel County and Northeast Highlands. In\nsoutheast New Mexico, Chaves County Plains.\n\n* WHEN...Through late tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Another round of showers and thunderstorms are expected to impact\nareas that observed rainfall yesterday and last night. With\nadditional rainfall amounts of 1 to 2 inches and localized\namounts of 2 to 3 inches, the areas that were recently impacted\nby heavy rainfall will be especially susceptible to additional\nflash flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/abq/EmergencyPrepFlood",
